Link .rela.plt only to .dynsym and leave sh_link 0 when there is none, as lld does. In
static executables it pointed at .symtab, which llvm-objcopy rejects for an allocated
relocation section, so splitting debug info out of dash-static failed.

Merged as wild-linker/wild#2750 (cf90616) after 0.10.0, which it does not apply to as is.

--- a/libwild/src/elf.rs
+++ b/libwild/src/elf.rs
@@ -5517,7 +5517,7 @@
             ty: sht::RELA,
             section_flags: shf::ALLOC.with(shf::INFO_LINK),
             element_size: C::RELA_ENTRY_SIZE,
-            link: &[output_section_id::DYNSYM, output_section_id::SYMTAB_LOCAL],
+            link: &[output_section_id::DYNSYM],
             min_alignment: C::RELA_ENTRY_ALIGNMENT,
             ..Self::DEFAULT_DEFS
         };
